From 03ba0e4c3ef3afa9d70ef63bf0109a29af2b04cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A session's first read goes on the wire before its open view
 and its queue read, since a runtime answers a session's reads one at a time
 in arrival order and the first read, which resolved the session's home twice,
 was sent last and waited behind both: startSessionReads resolves the home
 once, sends the first read, then the open view and the central runtime read
 (SessionReads.firstSent), and every snapshot read asks for the queue once
 firstSent settles, so the open, gap and asleep paths no longer read the queue
 beside it; a traced 1 MiB first visit on the Linux benchmark host gets its
 first read's answer 25-31 ms after the press instead of 37-65 ms, first
 visits go from 117.0 to 98.0 ms (1 MiB) and 132.3 to 103.2 ms (8 MiB) against
 05c70d3c over two alternating 6-repetition runs each, and the app's line
 budget is the measured 107,826.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QtZVtcNTgBwKhSN8i2v1w2
