 - A session whose cloud workspace goes asleep while the session is open (the catalog row turns stopped, from a stream's refusal or a `cloudWorkspaceChanged` notice) reads its snapshot and queue again (`rereadWhenAsleep`, `transcript/snapshot.ts`): a stopped workspace's reads come from the stored copy and answer no runtime fact, so a `session_not_found` read while its machine was being lost stops hiding the composer, whose placement notice says asleep and offers Wake, with why the server stopped it when the catalog names a reason (a runtime that stopped answering). Waking reads nothing here: the session's stream reconnects and raises its own gap.
